messages:
leah: opened a tiny PR to tighten SOC2 audit-log wording, replace 'permanent' with 'indefinite', add a Rust SDK snippet for export/redaction, and fix a CLI anchor that was 404. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/628
owen: nice. couple asks: 1) explicitly say exports don't change tenant TTLs; 2) call out which roles can request exports/holds. auditors asked for explicit RBAC text.
leah: drafted: 'Exports are immutable snapshots and do not modify the configured retention TTL for stored logs. Only Organization Admins and users assigned the Compliance role may request exports, place or release legal holds, or change retention settings.' switched wording to 'indefinite' where we previously used 'permanent'.
ram: please add a short migration hint mapping old_event.user -> actor.identity and mention we preserve legacy event_id for traceability. also include a one-line legal-hold release workflow for auditors.
legal-ops: wording looks fine. add a link to internal retention policy for evidence: https://internal/legal/retention-policy. and confirm that export requests are logged with requester.id in the audit trail.
leah: added internal link and the audit-note. added Rust snippet + minimal error example for redaction not enabled (customers asked about failure modes). snippet:
```rust
// Rust example (unique)
let req = ExportRequest { tenant_id: "acme".into(), start: "2024-01-01".into(), end: "2024-06-30".into(), redact_pii: true };
let resp = client.export_audit_logs(req).await?;
// error -> 422 {"error":"redaction_not_configured"}
```
owen: tiny nit: make the Rust boolean field snake_case to match SDK naming (redact_pii). also update the CLI anchor to /docs/cli#audit-export (previous link was /docs/cli/export).
leah: updated snippet and fixed CLI anchor. sdk-bot: PR 628 updated, link-check passed, staging build green.
leah: planning to merge tomorrow AM if legal-ops confirms. thanks everyone :thumbsup:
